!!! 10-concurrency-and-time.matrix
!!! Bounded structured parallelism and clock operations.
!!!
!!! "apply W across I" is Ny's parallel_map, with the whole contract intact:
!!! a statically resolved, nongeneric worker with exactly one scalar parameter
!!! and one scalar result; an input array of the parameter type; deterministic
!!! result order; at most 1,048,576 inputs.
!!!
!!! A worker and its entire transitive call graph may use scalar arithmetic,
!!! bitwise operations, comparisons, scalar casts, locals, branches, loops and
!!! direct calls to other isolated scalar helpers. They may NOT touch
!!! globals, pointers, owned buffers, views, record handles, arrays, text,
!!! class methods, a nested apply, assembly, foreign calls, console or file
!!! I/O, process operations, clocks, sleeps or fault payloads. These are
!!! checked on NIL as well, so hand-written NIL cannot grant extra effects.
!!!
!!! This is a scalar data-parallel facility. It is not an async runtime, a
!!! thread API, or a channels system. There are no task handles to forget to
!!! join: the caller receives the result array only after every worker thread
!!! has finished.

book tour.parallel

!!! An isolated scalar worker.
encode receives pixel as number returns number begin paragraph
    give (pixel bitwise xor 255) plus 3
end paragraph

!!! An isolated scalar helper the worker may call.
clamp receives sample as number returns number begin paragraph
    when sample is less than 0 then
        give 0
    end when
    give sample
end paragraph

normalise receives sample as number returns number begin paragraph
    give clamp with sample being (sample minus 1)
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph

    value pixels as array of number is [1 becomes number, 2 becomes number, 3 becomes number]

    !!! Results occupy the same indices as their inputs. The input array is
    !!! not mutated. A worker failure is a runtime error reported at the
    !!! lowest failing input index after every thread is joined; it is not a
    !!! catchable fault and no partial result array is returned.
    value encoded is apply encode across pixels
    say encoded at 0
    say encoded at 1
    say encoded at 2

    value normalised is apply normalise across pixels
    say normalised at 0

    !!! An empty input returns an empty array without starting a worker.
    value nothing_to_do as array of number is []
    value empty is apply normalise across nothing_to_do
    say the length of empty

    !!! Clock operations. A nonpositive duration is an immediate no-op.
    !!! Real and text durations are rejected rather than converted.
    value started as number is now in milliseconds
    sleep for 10 milliseconds
    value finished as number is now in milliseconds
    say finished is at least started

    give 0
end paragraph
